  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tuwekeze Pamoja: Working together to give children in Tanzania a better start to</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For a child growing up in rural Tanzania the chance of staying in school and achieving the grades needed to go to secondary school is low. This project aims to give children from birth to age 6 the best possible start to life by working with parents, schools, communities and government to promote a safe and conducive environment for learning - at home and school. There is a large investment in research to understand what inputs at this early age really make a difference, with an opportunity to influence government policy and wider practice in early childhood development. As a result of the project, children will be able to thrive and fulfil their potential.</narrative>
  </description>
